// D1773 — a `type` alias whose body is a NEGATION. `singleAliasMemberTyIx`'s ladder over the
// member's arena kind had no `TyNeg` arm, so the alias was not transparent, registered as a
// one-variant union, and the cell became the union BOX while the value stayed a bare scalar:
// `vl check` rc 0 and `(global $global$0 (mut (ref $1)) (i32.const 5))`.
//
// The INLINE spelling `!string` is the control and always ran at module scope. Both spellings
// refuse at a LOCAL binding, before and after, which is a separate pre-existing gap — a
// negation-annotated local takes no rep from its initializer — and not this row's.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type N = !string
// @@VALUE@@
5
// @@TYPE@@
N
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
5
